\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The disposition chain against the mask half-width, in the stellar rest frame. All 56{} threshold crossings are classified at every half-width, so the first two columns are what the mask costs and the last four are what it decides: how many crossings a catalogued transition of a masked species accounts for, how many it does not, how many of those outrank all 512{} control positions in their own window, and how many of \emph  {those} recur in a later epoch covering the same frequency. The adopted half-width is in bold.}}{22}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
